                        "entry_id": "735a9030-175c-3aeb-bd1c-b7041fa79a96",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state or characteristic of being salacious."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb16af7b-db6c-4b32-91e8-68a9829c42b6",
                                "sense_id": "fb61fe33-2776-33bb-ac51-d3e9e77bf8a0",
                                "text": "The cock, from his salaciousness, is allowed to be a short lived animal; but how long these birds live, if left to themselves, is not yet well ascertained by any historian."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0233e17-3b41-481c-ab65-bcc479251b8a",
                                "sense_id": "fb61fe33-2776-33bb-ac51-d3e9e77bf8a0",
                                "text": "[…] he began a tale which cannot be retold here, but which delighted the boys as much by its salaciousness as by its vivacity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0acb2011-043c-4881-932e-fea2fdd45b3b",
                                "sense_id": "fb61fe33-2776-33bb-ac51-d3e9e77bf8a0",
                                "text": "I giggle with the most revolting salaciousness over La Vie Parisienne, when I get hold of one in Chicago, yet I shouldn’t even try to hold your hand."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f20ce28c-c431-40e3-90a9-42d13e77d0e9",
                                "sense_id": "fb61fe33-2776-33bb-ac51-d3e9e77bf8a0",
                                "text": "Fokine did not mince words in describing the infamous closing moments of the ballet [L’Après-midi d’un faune], charging that Diaghilev used Nijinski as nothing more than a tool to shock his audience. He hinted that scandal was Diaghilev’s goal, for salaciousness would attract an audience."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "81b54703-d3b9-43b8-b3f0-198811380084",
                                "sense_id": "fb61fe33-2776-33bb-ac51-d3e9e77bf8a0",
                                "text": "[…] he actually used the word erotic, snagging his tongue on it as though the salaciousness of the syllables themselves was enough to arouse him […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
